[center][size=20pt][b]Remnant Retribution[/b][/size]
[i]v0.3.1 - a late-game colony crisis - for Starsector 0.98a-RC5[/i][/center]

[hr]

You've spent the campaign hunting Remnant Nexuses for their cores and blueprints. The machines noticed.

[b]Remnant Retribution[/b] is a standalone, vanilla-only colony crisis: every Remnant warship you destroy - and above all every [b]Nexus[/b] - raises the surviving network's threat assessment of your polity, until it marshals a retaliatory strike against your colonies. The more of the network you've torn down, the weaker its reach... right up until you kill the last Nexus and it throws everything left at you in one final convergence.

[hr]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pogoman/RemnantRetribution/main/screenshots/crisis_intel.png[/img][/center]

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Download[/b][/size]

[url=https://github.com/pogoman/RemnantRetribution/releases/download/v0.3.1/RemnantRetribution-0.3.1.zip]RemnantRetribution-0.3.1.zip[/url]

Extract into your Starsector [tt]mods/[/tt] folder and enable it in the launcher.

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]How the grudge builds[/b][/size]

Every Remnant hull your fleet destroys, anywhere in the sector, feeds the network's "grudge":

[list]
[li]Frigate - [b]1[/b][/li]
[li]Destroyer - [b]2[/b][/li]
[li]Cruiser - [b]4[/b][/li]
[li]Capital - [b]8[/b][/li]
[li][b]Remnant Nexus - 150[/b] (the single biggest contributor)[/li]
[/list]

As the grudge climbs:
[list]
[li]The colony crisis bar ticks up after every battle ("Remnant forces destroyed: +N"), plus a monthly trickle while the network plans.[/li]
[li]Remnant hunter-killer groups begin patrolling your systems.[/li]
[li]Around the crisis bar's minor-event stage, a [b]reconnaissance-in-force[/b] probes one of your colony systems - a few fleets raiding and assessing, no bombardment. The network's warning shot.[/li]
[li]Then the retaliation.[/li]
[/list]

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]The retaliation - and how to beat it[/b][/size]

When the crisis fires, a large strike force launches from the nearest surviving Nexus and descends on one of your colonies to [b]saturation-bomb it on arrival[/b]. This is a live event, not an abstract dice roll: the armada flies to your colony, and if you intercept and destroy it in your own system first, nothing is bombed.

[b]Better yet - avert it at the source.[/b] The moment a retaliation becomes impending, it marshals from a specific surviving Nexus, and [b]that Nexus's location is revealed on your map[/b]. Race there and destroy it [i]before the fleet launches[/i] and the retaliation is cancelled outright - no strike at all. (If the network is already reduced to dormant systems with no destructible Nexus, there's nothing to pre-empt and the strike comes anyway.)

Defeat the retaliation force and the grudge is halved - but each strike you beat makes the next one stronger. Machines don't forgive.

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Fragment the network - or end it for good[/b][/size]

The sector generates with roughly 8-15 live Nexus stations. Each one you destroy permanently weakens the network: monthly progress, hunter-killer presence, and strike strength all scale down with the surviving-Nexus fraction, to a configurable floor (default 25%).

Destroy the [b]last[/b] Nexus and the shattered network converges for one final, oversized strike (default 1.5x the normal cap). Defeat it and the crisis ends [b]permanently[/b] - the factor retires and no further grudge accrues. Lose it and the fragments fight on at the floor, every later strike another final convergence - defeat any one of them and the war still ends.

Prefer the old cruelty? Turn off [i]Permanent Neutralization Possible[/i] for the classic eternal grudge.

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Spoils of the hunt[/b][/size]

Where there is danger, there is opportunity. Every Nexus you bring down is also loot - all three rewards are on by default and individually toggleable:

[list]
[li][b]Gate Control Fragments[/b] - each destroyed Nexus drops a fragment of its Domain-era gate control core in the battle salvage. Take one to any dormant Gate and choose [i]Repair the Gate[/i]: that single Gate comes online - no Academy questline required, but no free sector-wide network either. The first repair also yields a working [b]Janus Device[/b] (needed to actually transit).[/li]
[li][b]Domain-era planetkiller[/b] - the [i]last[/i] Remnant Nexus guards a planetkiller; destroying it adds the weapon to the salvage (once per campaign, skipped if the vanilla questline already produced one).[/li]
[li][b]Path handover[/b] - while you carry the planetkiller, an intel entry offers surrendering it to the Luddic Path for the permanent vanilla pather agreement: holy peace, cells stand down for good.[/li]
[/list]

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

Everything above is tunable. With [url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=25658.0][b]LunaLib[/b][/url] enabled (optional) you get a live in-game settings menu (Shift+F2) - point values, thresholds, fleet strength, the neutralization rules, all of it. Without LunaLib the mod reads the same values from [tt]data/config/settings.json[/tt] and runs fine standalone.

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Requirements & compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[li][b]Starsector 0.98a-RC5[/b][/li]
[li][b]LunaLib[/b] - optional, for the in-game config menu[/li]
[li]Vanilla-only - no other hard dependencies[/li]
[li]Safe to [b]add[/b] to an existing save[/li]
[li][b]Removing[/b] it from a save with the crisis active will break that save - standard for crisis mods[/li]
[/list]

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]v0.3.1[/b]
[list]
[li]Fixed the Nexus trace never advancing past its first target: revealed Nexus intel was not being ticked by the game, so a destroyed Nexus was never noticed and no further Nexus was ever traced. Existing saves are repaired on load.[/li]
[li]Fixed the Path handover not granting a lasting agreement: it now sets the permanent pather agreement correctly (working around a vanilla expiry bug), credits the colony crisis bar, calls off any Path attack already in motion, and grants the reputation the vanilla handover does. The intel entry now clears itself cleanly instead of lingering. Existing saves are repaired on load.[/li]
[/list]

[b]v0.3.0[/b]
[list]
[li]The retaliation force now saturation-bombs the target colony [b]on arrival[/b] as a live, interceptable event, instead of resolving abstractly on a timer.[/li]
[li]Impending retaliations marshal from a specific surviving Nexus whose location is revealed - [b]destroy it before launch to avert the strike entirely[/b].[/li]
[/list]

[b]v0.2.0[/b]
[list]
[li]Network fragmentation & permanent neutralization; reconnaissance-in-force minor event; Nexus location tracing.[/li]
[/list]

